commit 3af76065946156ccd2a78d49076d68a546fb3d37

C03: a reply with nobody to answer asks the recipient; an addressee with nothing to say asks the text (MESSAGING1363)

Three open messaging literals reached no reader: «contestale que sí» and «contestale que llego en 10» (a reply with content but no addressee and no antecedent) and «escribile por whatsapp a Pedro» (recipient and channel, nothing to say). The closed incomplete-message grammar only knew forms that name a «mensaje/texto» or a channel-free conveyance.

effect_intent.resolve_explicit_clarification_intent: a reply head (contestale/respondele/contesta/responde/reply/answer) followed by «que/that» and content, without «a/to <someone>», is message.send missing the recipient; a write/send head with a channel (whatsapp/wsp/discord) and an addressee but no «que/that», colon or quoted content is message.send missing the message text. Nothing is sent: both are clarification contracts with no effect.

No .NET change. Offline probe only; tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


